# Everything the application image does not need.
#
# `frontend/` and `legacy-archive/` are together more than 1.5 GB. Without this
# file every `docker build` uploads them to the daemon before reading a single
# instruction, which turns a two-minute build into a ten-minute one and makes the
# build cache useless because the context hash changes whenever anyone touches a
# node_modules tree.
#
# `target/` is excluded deliberately rather than by accident: the image must be
# built from source inside the builder stage, never from whatever jar happens to
# be sitting on the machine that ran `docker build`. Several agents share this
# working tree and `target/` is frequently mid-write.

target/
frontend/
legacy-archive/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.vite/
docs/
tools/migration/
node_modules/

# Local configuration and anything that could carry a credential. Nothing here
# should ever exist in a repository, but an image is the wrong place to discover
# that it does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
application-local-secrets.yml
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.jks

.DS_Store
